                <head>219. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>During meetings in Washington November 19-21, 1969, Japanese Prime Minister
                        Sato and President Nixon discussed a wide range of matters of
                    mutual concern, including bilateral trade and textiles. See <ref
                        target="frus:frus1969-76v03/d30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1969–1976, volume III,
                        Document 30</ref>. Additional documentation on the Summit is scheduled for
                    publication in a forthcoming volume of <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                        Relations</hi>.</p>
            </div>
